{"t": 55.836, "n": 48, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I edited `docs/plans/i144.plan.md` in place to fix the trip-back reason, \"CST-AC5 is named by no test\". I ran no tests or checks.\n\n- **Cause:** a search for `CST-AC5` found no test that names it. The existing test of CST-B8, `test_machine_index_and_all_roots` in `tests/test_reports.py`, carries only `# CST-B8`. This task changed CST-B8 by dropping \", never removing it\".\n- **New requirement R10** (AC 3; CST-B8, CST-B17, CST-AC5): the machine index keeps marking a gone path `missing`, a reader leaves the entry in place, and only `stats forget` removes one.\n- **New test row 2.4** (Completed cell empty) in Phase 2, for `plugins/tempergraph/engine/tests/test_reports.py`, proving CST-AC5:\n  - It changes that test's comment to `# CST-B8, CST-AC5`.\n  - It adds one assertion that `rows.index_roots(home_path())` marks the gone entry `missing` while it is still listed.\n  - I placed it after test row 2.1 and before the code rows, so the test-first order holds.\n  - The other parts of CST-AC5 (duplicate sink name, thin projection, stale beat) are asserted by tests that already exist, and I left those alone.\n- **Status** is now `planned`. The six existing rows keep their `✓ 2026-11-25` marks, because I didn't change them.\n- **Section 0** now says I also opened `tests/test_reports.py` and why.\n- **Complexity:** `simple` still holds. The plan has 2 phases, 7 rows, 3 test rows, 7 files and 3 verification commands, and no phase is heavy. The proof table is unchanged, since it covers only the task's four criteria.\n\nARTIFACT plan: docs/plans/i144.plan.md\nARTIFACT complexity: simple", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "29b962a9-cb41-40d9-a6c7-2e2e7c575d2b"}
